## Framework-managed folders — don't hand-edit

⚠️ **`llm-wiki/how-to/` and `llm-wiki/best-practices/` are seeded by the framework on install** and may be overwritten when you re-run `install-wiki.ps1 -RefreshOnly` or `/new-wiki --sync` to pick up newer versions. If you edit these files in place, your changes get lost on the next refresh.

**Want to customize?** Put your additions in a separate location:

| Where it lives | What goes there | Survives refreshes? |
|---|---|---|
| `llm-wiki/how-to/` | Framework-shipped usage docs | ❌ Overwritten on refresh |
| `llm-wiki/best-practices/` | Framework-shipped best practices | ❌ Overwritten on refresh |
| `llm-wiki/wiki/best-practices/` | **Your project's** best practices (project-specific overrides + additions) | ✅ Yours forever |
| `llm-wiki/wiki/how-to/` (create if needed) | **Your project's** how-to docs (project-specific) | ✅ Yours forever |
| Anywhere else under `llm-wiki/wiki/` | Project-specific entries | ✅ Yours forever |

**Pattern**: if a shipped best-practice doesn't fit your project, copy it to `llm-wiki/wiki/best-practices/<same-name>.md` and edit the copy. The original stays at `llm-wiki/best-practices/<name>.md` (reference); your override lives at `llm-wiki/wiki/best-practices/<name>.md` (project canon). Document the divergence in your override's body so future-you remembers why.

(V2 will support proper user-override layering — for v1, the copy-elsewhere pattern is the workaround.)

## How-to folder

`how-to/` has short usage docs for the commands above. Start with `how-to/getting-started.md`. **Framework-managed** — see the warning above.

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or `_INDEX.md` — they're auto-generated by `wiki-map-compile.py` and `wiki-index-per-folder.py`
- Don't suppress contradictions in `wiki/` — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked, never delete the minority view
- Don't promote directly to `wiki/` — always stage through `wiki/_inbox/proposed/` and use `/wiki-promote` to move

